    "body": "## Motivation\n\nWith `--enable-priority-scheduling` and preemption on, a beam search request can corrupt other requests' KV cache.\n\n`PrefillAdder.preempt_to_schedule` picks victims from `running_batch.reqs`. A beam group's leader is one of them, so it can be chosen like any other request:\n\n1. `release_req` frees the leader's KV, and the leader is requeued through `preempt_list`.\n2. Nothing retires the group or frees its member rows. On the next decode, the member rows still ride the batch (`append_beam_tail`) and keep writing KV through rows that alias the leader's freed slots.\n3. Those slots have already been handed to other requests, so their KV is overwritten.\n\n`retract_decode` already handles this case: \"Beam groups cannot be retracted, so they are aborted instead of being requeued\". Preemption has no such branch.\n\nSymptoms I saw: tokens in another request's KV slots that only beam selection produced, the busy-time pool check (`Full Pool Mem Leak Detected!`), and, in one run, `AssertionError: Only a mamba-capable tree cache allows freeing before alloc` on a full-attention model.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `preempt_to_schedule`: do not consider beam group leaders as preemption victims. A higher-priority request then preempts other requests, or waits. Preemption is optional here, unlike retraction under memory pressure, so I kept the group running rather than aborting it.\n- `test_prefill_adder.py`:\n  - `create_mock_req` sets `beam_group = None`; a `spec=Req` mock would otherwise return a truthy mock attribute.\n  - New tests: the only lower-priority request is a beam leader, so preemption fails and nothing is released; a plain lower-priority request next to a beam leader is preempted instead of the leader.\n\n  Both fail on `main`.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot applicable. No model-side change.\n\n## Benchmarking and Profiling\n\nNot applicable.\n\nHow I tested: CPU only, no model, no server.\n\n- `test/registered/unit/managers/test_prefill_adder.py` on `main` (dba22e9b68): `2 failed, 54 passed` (the two new tests). With this change: `56 passed`.\n- I used a CPU scheduler driver that runs the real `Scheduler`, `PrefillAdder` and `BeamCoordinator` with fake logits derived from each KV row's contents, mixing beam and plain requests with priorities. The driver needs #46855 to get past member spawn, so both runs carry it. Over 60 seeds:\n  - without this change, 7 seeds fail the busy-time pool check. With that check off, other requests' KV is overwritten (4 CONTENT and 1 INPUT mismatches) and 3 seeds stall. Every failing seed has priority scheduling on;\n  - with it, all 60 pass in both modes.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit). I ran the repo's pre-commit hooks on the changed files.\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). Not needed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40623792293](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40623792293)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40623791169](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40623791169)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40623791096](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40623791096)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
